Z||000000||EdsB52||07-03-2001||02:28 PM||||I posted the following information and opinions last night in the following post:<P><BR>Hey kids, I’m back from lost wages (Las Vegas). After reading replies to my posts, I've decided to respond to the people who unreasonably slammed me in the good name of Archie. Mere disagreement with my opinion doesn't suffice as entry into this registry, just blatant, derogatory, defamatory responses to me because you want to appear as one of Archie's girls.<P>The "Take Archie out of your mouth" list is as follows:<P>001E<BR>Wannabe<BR>sjp777<BR>TriAD<BR>Tryxalon<BR>gtcash<BR>voyagerspe<P>If you don't like this, or don't like / hate me, so what? You will undoubtedly further this dissention by responding in a like manor, which illustrates your mutual culpability, but will adamantly deny you are participatory. If you find this defamatory, realize I'm not identifying you by given name, just by moniker, so you can maintain anonymity by non self-disclosure.<P>Archie wrote;<P>“This, like anything else that is posted to the Internet, becomes a permanent record on some server somewhere. E, & E et al, as you try to make jerks out of yourselves, remember that 5 years from now, When you've grown up, your actions today will still be available for others to read.”<P>Oh, I see what he means.<P>“BTW, what are you smoking tonight?”<BR>					Archie<P>Now one of the people in that post emailed me not to necessarily apologize, but to agree in part with my position. I don't know what his moniker is so I cannot remove him from the above list. The purpose of this repost is to illustrate two things; first, censorship is present even in a supposedly casual forum such as this. Second, politics are present and even prevalent in a forum such as this. And it feels like economic politics more than conventional politics where people persuade others through friendship for non-pecuniary gain. I think my contention is supported by this example; when one of the girls in the forum was being tossed around, I believe Fierolisa or ?, the topic was closed but not removed. The post above was removed within minutes or hours of original posting. I don't know the relationship between Cliff and Archie, but I now know that economic politics play a part in this club.<P>Now Cliff, you can remove this post, you can ban me from the club, you can even report me to Yahoo or whom ever you want. But you will never successfully sensor me, so let this post stand and go away. All you're doing by removing my posts is substantiating my contentions. I'm not trying to harm your commercial enterprise, just merely defend my position. I could email everyone in the club with this information from an anonymous computer, so don't think you can shut me up. Just answer this; why did you remove my post? And when you answer that, distinguish why you just closed the other post that defamed or objectified the female member, and why you didn't remove it like you did my post referring to Archie and his supporters. Please, make some cents out of your explanation, as in dollars and cents. "Gee I don't know," or "I screwed up," or "I guess I should have" don't work Cliff, you're not stupid, in fact I believe you're pretty sharp. Admit this club is based on commerce and not casual Fiero conversation and I'll believe you, if not convince me otherwise.||||reg||1
